ofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor - Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Apply now Description The Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions in Creighton University’s College of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor level beginning in August 2027. Rank will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. We seek an outstanding teacher-scholar who is committed to excellence and innovation in undergraduate education, student-centered learning, and meaningful faculty mentorship. The successful candidate will teach foundational and advanced undergraduate courses based on departmental needs. Possible teaching assignments include human anatomy and physiology, human pathophysiology, exercise physiology, exercise prescription, nutrition, fitness and wellness, and statistics and research design. Additional responsibilities include mentoring and advising students and providing service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. The successful candidate will establish and sustain an active, independent research program that complements departmental strengths and provides meaningful opportunities for undergraduate students to participate in study design, data collection, analysis, presentation, and publication. We particularly encourage candidates whose scholarship addresses one or more of the following areas: exercise immunology, physiological stress responses, and immunoendocrine interactions; skeletal muscle adaptation, neuromuscular function, muscle fatigue, and resistance-training adaptations across the lifespan; translational research connecting basic physiological mechanisms with applications in aging, rehabilitation, or chronic disease management; and innovative quantitative or integrative approaches in exercise and human physiology, including advanced modeling, health informatics, or multiscale physiological analysis. Research programs using human participants, animal models, or both are welcomed, and candidates whose work bridges multiple levels of physiological organization are especially encouraged to apply. Qualifications A Ph.D. in exercise science, physiology, or a closely related field is required by the beginning of the appointment Evidence of, or strong potential for, excellence in undergraduate teaching and educational innovation Potential to establish an active, independent, and externally visible research program involving undergraduate students Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor level must demonstrate a record of teaching, scholarship, and service appropriate to that rank Ability to foster student learning, development, and decision-making in support of students’ goals, success, wellness, and needs Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse populations Empathy and compassion for the experiences of others Application Instructions Candidates should submit their application through Interfolio. When prompted, please upload the following: Cover letter addressing interest in the position and relevant teaching and research experience Current curriculum vitae Candidates selected for an interview will be required to provide: Original academic transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (photocopies are acceptable during the initial application process) Three letters of recommendation, at least two of which should address the candidate’s teaching ability Statement of teaching philosophy Research statement describing the candidate’s plans for an active research program and undergraduate student involvement A one-page statement describing the candidate’s potential contributions to Creighton’s mission ( https://www.creighton.edu/about/mission-history and https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/about/about-our-mission ) Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further information, please visit the Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions website at https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/exercisescience. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Jake Siedlik, Associate Professor, Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions, at JakeSiedlik@creighton.edu. For questions or issues submitting application materials, please contact HR@creighton.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department Exercise Sciences Department Posted Fri, 09/11/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close