Provost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Non-Tenure Track Assistant Professor - Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Apply now Description The Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions in Creighton University’s College of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning in January or August 2027. We seek an outstanding teacher who is committed to excellence in undergraduate education, student engagement, and student-centered learning. The successful candidate will primarily teach multiple sections of EXS 111 Fundamentals of Human Anatomy and EXS 112 Fundamentals of Human Physiology each academic year. These foundational courses support the undergraduate nursing curriculum and serve students preparing for nursing and other health professions. The successful candidate will be especially attentive to the needs of first-year undergraduate students transitioning to college-level science coursework. Additional responsibilities include maintaining regular student office hours, participating in departmental meetings and service activities, and contributing to a collaborative academic environment consistent with Creighton University’s Catholic, Jesuit mission and values. Candidates should demonstrate excellent communication skills, a commitment to high-quality instruction, the ability to foster student success in large foundational courses, and support for the University’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. The Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions has experienced substantial enrollment growth in recent years and plays an increasingly important role in supporting the curricula of the College of Nursing and other health professions programs. EXS 111 and EXS 112 generate significant annual student credit hours and are central to the University’s commitment to high-quality undergraduate education. Qualifications A master’s degree in exercise science, anatomy, physiology, biology, or a closely related field is required; a terminal degree is preferred Prior experience teaching undergraduate anatomy and physiology is strongly preferred Evidence of, or strong potential for, excellence in undergraduate teaching and educational innovation, particularly in large foundational science courses Ability to engage and support first-year students and students preparing for nursing and other health professions Ability to foster student learning, development, and decision-making in support of students’ goals, success, wellness, and needs Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse populations Empathy and compassion for the experiences of others Application Instructions Candidates should submit their application through Interfolio. When prompted, please upload the following: Cover letter addressing interest in the position and relevant teaching experience Current curriculum vitae A one-page statement describing teaching philosophy Sample syllabi Samples of student and peer teaching evaluations if available Contact information for three professional references Candidates selected for an interview will be required to provide: Original academic transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (photocopies are acceptable during the initial application process) A one-page statement describing the candidate’s potential contributions to Creighton’s mission ( https://www.creighton.edu/about/mission-history and https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/about/about-our-mission ) Three letters of recommendation, at least two of which should address the candidate’s teaching ability Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further information, please visit the Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions website at https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/exercisescience. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Mitchel Magrini, Associate Professor, Department of Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions, at MtichelMagrini@creighton.edu. For questions or issues submitting application materials, please contact HR@creighton.edu. About Creighton At Creighton, we offer meaningful work driven by a 475-year-old Jesuit tradition committed to social justice and serving others. Through this tradition, we push the boundaries on innovation. We pursue new knowledge for the betterment of society. We seek to improve our world through Catholic and Jesuit values. Omaha is a diverse community of 850,000 with four Fortune 500 companies, an active sports scene, and a vibrant arts community. Recent Wall Street Journal/Times Higher Education College rankings recognized Creighton University among the top 20% of institutions in its survey and among the Top 10 big-city colleges in the Midwest. Creighton University also ranks in the top third of National Universities in U.S. News & World Report and was previously recognized for 16 years in a row as No. 1 among Best Regional Universities–Midwest. Over the past 17 years, Creighton is the No. 1 Goldwater-producing Catholic university in the country and in the top 20 of private universities producing Goldwater Scholars over the past decade. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department Exercise Sciences Department Posted Fri, 09/11/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
