ovost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Tenure Track Assistant Professor - Political Science and International Relations Apply now Description The department of Political Science and International Relations at Creighton University invites applications for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor specializing in American Politics. We seek individuals committed to being outstanding teacher-scholars within a primarily undergraduate-serving college. The successful applicant will teach a 3-3 course load that includes 1 st year core courses in American government and politics, as well as upper division elective courses in their area of expertise, including American institutions, behavior and research methods , depending on departmental needs. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Political Science (or a closely related field) is required to be in hand by the beginning of the contract (August 1, 2027) An emerging record of scholarship Ability to foster student learning, development, and decision making in support of their goals, success, wellness, and needs Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to develop rapport quickly and effectively with a diversity of populations Empathy and compassion for the experiences of others Application Instructions Candidates should submit their application through Interfolio. When prompted please upload the following: Cover letter Current curriculum vitae If a candidate is called for an interview, they will be required to provide: Original academic transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (photocopies acceptable during initial application process) A scholarly writing sample Three letters of recommendation, at least two of which should speak to the candidate’s teaching ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy A one-page statement describing the candidate’s potential contributions to Creighton’s mission ( https://www.creighton.edu/about/mission-history and https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/about/about-our-mission ) Review of completed applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For further information, please visit department website here If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact Dr. Erika Moreno, Chair of the Department of Political Science and International Relations ( erikamoreno@creighton.edu ). For questions or issues submitting your application or materials, please don’t hesitate to contact HR@creighton.edu . About Creighton At Creighton, we offer meaningful work driven by a 475-year old Jesuit tradition committed to social justice and serving others. Through this tradition, we push the boundaries on innovation. We pursue new knowledge for the betterment of society. We seek to improve our world through Catholic and Jesuit values. Omaha is a diverse community of 850,000 with four Fortune-500 companies, an active sports scene, and a vibrant arts community. Recent Wall Street Journal/Times Higher Education College rankings recognized Creighton University among the top 20% of institutions in its survey and among the Top 10 big-city colleges in the Midwest. Creighton University also ranks in the top third of National Universities in U.S. News & World Report’s and was previously recognized for 16 years in a row as No. 1 among Best Regional Universities – Midwest. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department Political Science & International Relations Department Posted Fri, 07/31/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
