ce of the Provost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Non-Tenure Track Assistant Professor - Fine and Performing Arts - Theatre/Technical Director Apply now Description Creighton University’s Department of Fine & Performing Arts invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Theatre, beginning in January 2027. Candidates should have experience teaching at the undergraduate level. In addition to assuming responsibility for technical direction and production management for up to four productions per years, candidates will teach a 2-2 undergraduate course load based upon experience and departmental needs, including lighting design and upper-level courses. We prefer candidates with interest in community engagement, service learning, and especially teaching theatre. Additionally, we are looking for candidates who can foster student learning, development, and decision making in support of their goals, success, wellness, and needs. Qualifications M.F.A. in Theatre or closely related degree such as Technical Direction required Candidates with interest in community engagement, service learning, and teaching theatre preferred 2-4 years of professional experience in scenic construction, structural engineering for the stage and rigging Advanced skills in theatrical drafting software (Vectorworks or AutoCAD) Prior experience teaching or a demonstrated ability to instruct and safely manage undergraduate students in a technical environment Proven ability to manage multi-venue calendars, student labor pools, and complex materials budgets Ability to foster student learning, development, and decision making in support of their goals, success, wellness, and needs Evidence of excellent college level teaching preferred Empathy and compassion for the experiences of others Application Instructions Candidates should submit the following through Interfolio. When prompted, please upload the following: Letter of intent or Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vitae One-page Statement of Teaching Philosophy If a candidate is called for an interview, they will be required to provide: Examples of recent work (designs, renderings, etc.) A one-page statement describing the candidate’s potential contributions to Creighton’s mission ( https://www.creighton.edu/about/mission-history and https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/about/about-our-mission ) Original academic transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended (photocopies acceptable during initial application process) Three letters of recommendation, at least two of which should speak to the candidate’s teaching ability Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further information, please visit https://www.creighton.edu/arts-sciences/fineandperformingarts/ . If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact Dr. Fred Hanna, Chair of the Department of Fine and Performing Arts ( FredHanna@creighton.edu ). For questions or issues submitting your application or materials, please don’t hesitate to contact HR@creighton.edu . About Creighton Omaha is a diverse community of 850,000 with four Fortune-500 companies, an active sports scene, and a vibrant arts community. Recent Wall Street Journal/Times Higher Education College rankings recognized Creighton University among the top 20% of institutions in its survey and among the Top 10 big-city colleges in the Midwest. Creighton University also ranks in the top third of National Universities in U.S. News & World Report’s and was previously recognized for 16 years in a row as No. 1 among Best Regional Universities – Midwest. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department Fine & Performing Arts Department Posted Wed, 07/15/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
