rthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Special Faculty Special Instructor/Lab/EMS/Paramedicine Apply now Description The Department of Paramedicine at Creighton University invites applications and nominations for a Special Instructor/Lab position, in the Department of Paramedicine . Special Instructors are part-time faculty members, compensated by the University, who perform University teaching in lab, and/or simulation. This position will help to instruct EMS students per program policies and procedures, facilitating classroom and laboratory sessions. Depending on changing Department of Paramedicine needs, other responsibilities, assignments, and tasks may be added. These instructors shall perform duties at less than 50% of the workload of full-time faculty and shall have their agreed-upon workload percentage clearly specified in their letter of appointment. Qualifications 2 years of patient care experience in an emergency or critical care environment, preferably including field experience in the delivery of out-of-hospital emergency care Candidates must possess or be eligible for licensure as a paramedic and EMS Instructor designation in the State of Nebraska. Current provider and instructor certifications in BLS, ACLS, PALS, PEPP, AMLS, ITLS, and PHTLS preferred Participation in supportive faculty development programs Application Instructions Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department College of Nursing - Paramedicine Posted Wed, 11/05/2025 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
