and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Special Faculty Special Faculty - Psych/Mental Health Apply now Description Join Creighton University as a Special Faculty member to help teach students how to become compassionate nurses!  College of Nursing in Phoenix, AZ is hiring experienced Registered Nurses who are committed to excellence and quality patient care.  Our NCLEX pass rates are above the Arizona and National average! Provide direct supervision of students in the clinical areas. Oversee Labs and Simulations. Hours vary week to week depending on the number of sections in the lab. Special Faculty typically work 12-18 hours per week. Clinical rotations are 8 weeks. Spring Term 1 (Jan - March) Summer Term (June - July) Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) (or earned doctorate in nursing) OR possess a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) and be currently enrolled in a MSN program to be considered Minimum of two (2) years in nursing and in the specialty role. Prior teaching in a clinical setting preferred. A current unencumbered license as an RN in the state of Arizona, or eligibility for licensure Application Instructions When applying : Applicants/Candidates are asked to provide a Resume/Curriculum Vitae and a Statement/Cover letter indicating why you wish to be considered for a teaching role. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department College of Nursing - Phoenix Posted Wed, 07/30/2025 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate Select Language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Arm