Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Assistant/Associate Professor- Team Leader - General Dentistry Apply now Description Creighton University School of Dentistry is seeking two motivated individuals as Team Leaders within the School's pre doctorial clinic model. The 12-month, non-tenure, Clinician Educator track appointments will work with a team of dedicated faculty who are building on a rich legacy of excellence in dental education in the Department of General Dentistry Position responsibilities include: Serving as a Team leader in the school’s comprehensive team-based practice model as well as supporting the delivery of the curriculum in preclinical courses and labs. Administrative management of students within an assigned team and overseeing the clinical care of their patient families as the students matriculate toward graduation. Participation in scholarly activity and service is encouraged as part of the position responsibilities. Qualifications DDS or DMD degree, Document successful completion of Part I and Part II of the National Board Dental Examination or the Integrated National Board Dental Examination prior to the date of hire Must possess or obtain and maintain an unrestricted Nebraska Dental License in the category for which they are eligible along with subsequent credentialing from applicable third-party payer systems . Candidates must also possess strong organizational and communication skills with a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a collegial, interdisciplinary environment. Preferred: Private Practice experience is preferred but not mandatory Application Instructions How to apply Candidates should submit their application through Interfolio The Complete application must include: Cover Letter CV or Resume If a candidate is called for an interview, they may be asked to provide one or all of the following: Original academic transcripts from all institutions of higher education attended Letters of recommendation, at least two of which should speak to the candidate’s teaching ability Statement of teaching philosophy as it applies to dental education Make formal presentation to faculty body a sample of scholarly activity Creighton University is a Catholic and Jesuit comprehensive university committed to excellence in undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. The School of Dentistry provides an exceptional education in an unrivaled clinical learning environment and is an integral component of Creighton University, a dynamic and growing institution located in Omaha Nebraska, and a proud member of the Big East Conference. Omaha boasts a lively, thriving metropolitan community conveniently located in the nation’s heartland. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department School of Dentistry Posted Wed, 03/26/2025 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighto