Community Standards Faith, Service and Justice Campus Ministry Schlegel Center for Service and Justice Worship, Prayer and Sacraments Retreat Center Deglman Center Well-being and Safety Physical Wellness Emotional Wellness Campus Safety Cura Services Clubs and Organizations Fraternities and Sororities Club Sports Multicultural Student Organizations Creighton Students Union Honor Societies Dining About About Overview Learn about Creighton’s rich history, commitment to Jesuit, Catholic values, and dedication to academic excellence. Family & Parents Mission and History What Is a Jesuit Education? Creighton’s History Community and Belonging Commitment to Service Sustainability at Creighton Jesuit Community Rankings and Recognition Outcomes Analytics and Institutional Research Office Leadership, Key Offices and Contacts Office of the President Office of the Provost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Special Faculty Special Faculty - Multiple Specialties Apply now Description Creighton University's College of Nursing (CON) is hiring Special Faculty for the Spring, Summer, and Fall sessions at the Omaha campus.  Well-qualified candidates will demonstrate a commitment to teaching, and practice, and be responsible to educate undergraduate nursing students. Applications accepted until positions are filled. Work in Safety & Quality labs and Health Assessment Lab (hours dependent upon the number of sections of lab from 2–18 hour/week) OR Clinical Rotations (varying from 12 – 18 hours/week) and requires direct supervision of students in the clinical areas. Medical / Surgical Psychiatric / Mental Health Critical Care Community Health Maternal / Child Pediatrics Qualifications Requirements: · Candidates must possess a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) (or earned doctorate in nursing) OR a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) and be currently enrolled in a MSN program. · A current unencumbered license as an RN in the state of Nebraska, or eligibility for license as required per state bound regulations for teaching across geographic boundaries required. · Two (2) years of continuous clinical experience. · Experience in classroom or clinical, and/or on-line instruction preferred. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: Clinical expertise in area of nursing; Excellent written/verbal communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills; Strong collaborative/teamwork ability to motivate, and inspire individuals at all levels of the organization; Ability to foster student and staff learning, development, and decision making in support of goals, success, wellness, and needs; Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to develop rapport quickly and effectively with a diversity of populations; Empathy and compassion for the experiences of others; Mission/Service and Results oriented; Ability to work at times non-traditional business hours when needed (i.e. weekends, evening, and/or holiday) Application Instructions How to Apply Applicants must apply with the following materials attached to the online application: • Curriculum Vitae • A statement indicating your top 3 nursing specialty interest areas and why. Candidates are strongly urged to familiarize themselves with Creighton’s mission and founding principles and review the Faculty Handbook and definition of “Special Faculty” at: https://www.creighton.edu/fileadmin/user/GeneralCounsel/docs/Faculty_Handbook_2020.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department College of Nursing - Omaha Posted Tue, 11/19/2024 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate Select Language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Armenian Azerbaijani Basque Belarusian Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Catalan Cebuano Chichewa Chinese (Simplified) Chinese (Traditional) Corsican Croatian Czech Danish Dutch English Esperanto Estonian Filipino Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Haitian Creole Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hmong Hungarian Icelandic Igbo Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Kannada Kazakh Khmer Korean Kurdish (Kurmanji) Kyrgyz Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Myanmar (Burmese) Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Romanian Russian Samoan Scottish Gaelic Serbian Sesotho Shona Sindhi Sinhala Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Sundanese Swahili Swedish Tajik Tamil Telugu Thai Turkish Ukraini