    "https://www.creighton.edu/assistant-professor-pharmacy-sciences-tenure-track-omaha": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Pharmacy Sciences, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Pharmacy Sciences, Tenure Track - Omaha | Creighton University Skip to main content Alumni Give Search Request Info Visit Apply Academics Admissions Cost & Aid Student Experience About Athletics Menu My Saved Programs Academics Academics Overview Blending rigorous coursework with hands-on learning, Creighton academics are carefully designed to prepare impactful leaders. Institutional Accreditation Office of the Registrar Degrees and Programs Magis Core Curriculum Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Accelerated Bachelor’s to Master’s Colleges and Schools College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing College of Professional and Continuing Education Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine School of Pharmacy and Health Professions Centers and Institutes Creighton Institute for Population Health Kingfisher Institute Global Education Global Scholars Program Study Abroad International Students and Scholars Health Sciences at Creighton Schools, Colleges and Programs Simulation Interprofessional Education Clinical Education Arizona Health Education Alliance Libraries Collections Services and Support Research at Creighton Student Success Academic Advising Academic Support Distinguished Scholars Program John P. Fahey Career Center Pre-Professional Advising Student Accessibility Services Student and Family Support Student Support Services (TRIO) Admissions Admissions Overview Experience our close community with a campus tour, connect with admissions counselors or apply now. Find Your Application Undergraduate Applications Graduate Applications New Student Portal Dates and Deadlines Admission Requirements Undergraduate and Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Non-Degree-Seeking Students Admitted Students Admitted Undergraduate Students Admitted Graduate Students Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Visits Graduate Visits Plan Your Omaha Visit Plan Your Phoenix Visit Undergraduate Admitted Student Day Graduate Admitted Student Day Undergraduate Events Near You Contact Admissions Contact Undergraduate Admissions Contact Graduate Admissions Our Student Body Info for Parents and Families Prospective Students Admitted Students Committed Students Current Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Overview Creighton is within your reach. Explore financial aid options, calculate your costs and discover scholarships. Tuition and Costs Net Price Calculator Undergraduate Tuition and Fees Graduate School Costs Summer and Winter Term Costs Applying for Aid Types of Financial Aid Scholarships Grants Loans Student Employment Military and Veterans Benefits Financial Aid Forms & Consumer Info Consumer Information and Policies Contact the Office of Financial Aid Student Experience Student Experience Overview Explore our vibrant campus life with diverse student activities, supportive resources and a strong sense of community. Housing First-Year Housing Process Off-Campus Housing Living-Learning Communities On-Campus Housing Building Community New Student Orientation An Inclusive Community Community Standards Faith, Service and Justice Campus Ministry Schlegel Center for Service and Justice Worship, Prayer and Sacraments Retreat Center Deglman Center Well-being and Safety Physical Wellness Emotional Wellness Campus Safety Cura Services Clubs and Organizations Fraternities and Sororities Club Sports Multicultural Student Organizations Creighton Students Union Honor Societies Dining About About Overview Learn about Creighton’s rich history, commitment to Jesuit, Catholic values, and dedication to academic excellence. Family & Parents Mission and History What Is a Jesuit Education? Creighton’s History Community and Belonging Commitment to Service Sustainability at Creighton Jesuit Community Rankings and Recognition Outcomes Analytics and Institutional Research Office Leadership, Key Offices and Contacts Office of the President Office of the Provost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Assistant Professor of Pharmacy Sciences, Tenure Track - Omaha Apply now Description Creighton University, a Catholic and Jesuit institution, is actively seeking applications for a full time (12 month) faculty position in our Pharmacy Sciences Department in Omaha, Nebraska. This position will be at the Assistant Professor level and will have a Tenure-Track appointment in the Department of Pharmacy Sciences. The successful candidate will join a team of professionals committed to innovation and excellence in education, scholarship, research and service within the Jesuit tradition. Creighton seeks a quality educator who is excited about competency-based education, dedicated to scholarship and research in their discipline/interest area, willing to collaborate and demonstrate effective teamwork, and embraces Jesuit values. Individuals with interest and experience in web-based education are especially encouraged to apply.  Responsibilities of the position include instruction to Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) students in the Omaha campus, Phoenix campus and distance pathways, and participation in graduate education. Creighton’s comprehensive Omaha Campus include health sciences academic disciplines in dentistry, medicine, nursing, physician assistant, occupational therapy, pharmacy, and physical therapy. Teaching & Educational Responsibilities: Primary teaching will be Pharmacology and related topics to Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) students and students in the masters’ and PhD tracks of Pharmaceutical Sciences Graduate Program. Secondary teaching may be Pharmacology and related topics to Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) and Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) students. Qualifications PhD in pharmacology or a closely related discipline. Expertise and experience in teaching pharmacology and related topics to Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) and graduate level (master’s and PhD) students is strongly preferred. A record of grant application submissions with potential for grant funding and peer-reviewed publications is required. Effective communication, organization, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills. Scholarship Responsibilities: The successful applicant will be expected to establish a robust basic or applied research laboratory. We are especially interested in candidates who investigate basic and translational topics of pharmacology and molecular biology relevant but not limited to cardiovascular diseases, cancer, neurological diseases, ocular diseases, or infectious diseases. The successful candidate will be provided with laboratory space and a start-up package to develop their independent research program. There are collaborative faculty with diverse interests and expertise, several core facilities, and various internal grant mechanisms to support initial research efforts. Faculty are expected to maintain scholarly activity appropriate to their rank.  Refer to the Faculty Handbook (link below) for more information. Service Responsibilities: The successful applicant will be expected to participate in department, program, school, university and professional service in accordance with the mission of Creighton University. Refer to the Faculty Handbook for more information. Application Instructions Expressions of interest and all applications will be treated in strict confidence.  The position is available July 1, 2027. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Application materials are to be submitted electronically and should include the following for the application to be considered complete: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae 1-page research statement 1-page teaching statement Contact information of four references. Once you have submitted your application, please send a brief email to the Search Committee Chair, E. Jeffrey North, PhD. at JeffreyNorth@creighton.edu . If you would like more information or have questions regarding the faculty position, please contact E. Jeffrey North, PhD. Candidates are strongly urged to familiarize themselves with: The Pharmacy Programs (Omaha, Distance, Phoenix), “One Creighton” mission and philosophy The Creighton University Faculty Handbook The Creighton University Mission and founding principles For information regarding Creighton University Benefits, please visit the Creighton University Benefit Guide Creighton University is a leading Jesuit education institution at the intersection of health and humanity. Founded in 1878, Creighton enrolls more than 8,000 students and is one of the 28 Jesuit colleges and universities in the U.S. Creighton is a world-class academic institution recognized for excellence in teaching, learning and research, and enriched by a centuries-long tradition of Jesuit, Catholic education with a low 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio, Creighton offers a close-knit, small-school feel with big-school opportunities and spirit. With over 140 academic paths spanning the arts, sciences, law, business and multiple health sciences fields, Creighton offers something for everyone. At Creighton, the classroom is just the beginning. From research to internships to service-based learning, our students do more. Omaha, Nebraska offers the perfect blend of cosmopolitan sophistication and suburban relaxation. Omaha boasts a thriving economy with a population of almost 1 million in the metro area. The city is home to four Fortune 500 companies, making it a major regional economic hub between Chicago, Denver, Kansas City, and Minneapolis. Omaha remains incredibly affordable, with the cost of living 8% lower than the national average. Most attractions, including the airport, are less than a 20-minute drive from Creighton. Omaha offers many amenities, from a thriving food scene, entertainment districts, the renowned-Henry Doorly Zoo and the all-new Peter Kiewit Luminarium. Omaha boasts world-class health care and excellent public and private education throughout the city. We are on the “Best” lists for affordability, livability, and opportunity. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department Pharmacy Sciences Department Posted Wed, 10/21/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
