      "title": "Assistant Dean for Evaluation & Analytics -School of Medicine",
      "description": "Assistant Dean for Evaluation & Analytics -School of Medicine | Creighton University Skip to main content Alumni Give Search Request Info Visit Apply Academics Admissions Cost & Aid Student Experience About Athletics Menu My Saved Programs Academics Academics Overview Blending rigorous coursework with hands-on learning, Creighton academics are carefully designed to prepare impactful leaders. Institutional Accreditation Office of the Registrar Degrees and Programs Magis Core Curriculum Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Accelerated Bachelor’s to Master’s Colleges and Schools College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing College of Professional and Continuing Education Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine School of Pharmacy and Health Professions Centers and Institutes Creighton Institute for Population Health Kingfisher Institute Global Education Global Scholars Program Study Abroad International Students and Scholars Health Sciences at Creighton Schools, Colleges and Programs Simulation Interprofessional Education Clinical Education Arizona Health Education Alliance Libraries Collections Services and Support Research at Creighton Student Success Academic Advising Academic Support Distinguished Scholars Program John P. Fahey Career Center Pre-Professional Advising Student Accessibility Services Student and Family Support Student Support Services (TRIO) Admissions Admissions Overview Experience our close community with a campus tour, connect with admissions counselors or apply now. Find Your Application Undergraduate Applications Graduate Applications New Student Portal Dates and Deadlines Admission Requirements Undergraduate and Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Non-Degree-Seeking Students Admitted Students Admitted Undergraduate Students Admitted Graduate Students Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Visits Graduate Visits Plan Your Omaha Visit Plan Your Phoenix Visit Undergraduate Admitted Student Day Graduate Admitted Student Day Undergraduate Events Near You Contact Admissions Contact Undergraduate Admissions Contact Graduate Admissions Our Student Body Info for Parents and Families Prospective Students Admitted Students Committed Students Current Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Overview Creighton is within your reach. Explore financial aid options, calculate your costs and discover scholarships. Tuition and Costs Net Price Calculator Undergraduate Tuition and Fees Graduate School Costs Summer and Winter Term Costs Applying for Aid Types of Financial Aid Scholarships Grants Loans Student Employment Military and Veterans Benefits Financial Aid Forms & Consumer Info Consumer Information and Policies Contact the Office of Financial Aid Student Experience Student Experience Overview Explore our vibrant campus life with diverse student activities, supportive resources and a strong sense of community. Housing First-Year Housing Process Off-Campus Housing Living-Learning Communities On-Campus Housing Building Community New Student Orientation An Inclusive Community Community Standards Faith, Service and Justice Campus Ministry Schlegel Center for Service and Justice Worship, Prayer and Sacraments Retreat Center Deglman Center Well-being and Safety Physical Wellness Emotional Wellness Campus Safety Cura Services Clubs and Organizations Fraternities and Sororities Club Sports Multicultural Student Organizations Creighton Students Union Honor Societies Dining About About Overview Learn about Creighton’s rich history, commitment to Jesuit, Catholic values, and dedication to academic excellence. Family & Parents Mission and History What Is a Jesuit Education? Creighton’s History Community and Belonging Commitment to Service Sustainability at Creighton Jesuit Community Rankings and Recognition Outcomes Analytics and Institutional Research Office Leadership, Key Offices and Contacts Office of the President Office of the Provost Administrative Offices Key Contacts Campus Locations, Maps and Parking Campus and Regional Locations Campus Maps Parking and Transportation News and Events Blog Creighton Magazine Media Coverage News Events Institutional Accreditation Academic and Non-Academic Accreditation Creighton Commitments Athletics Alumni Give Search Search Site Search Directory Filter by School College of Arts and Sciences College of Nursing, Omaha Campus College of Nursing, Phoenix Campus College of Professional and Continuing Education Creighton University Staff Heider College of Business School of Dentistry School of Law School of Medicine, Omaha Campus School of Medicine, Phoenix Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Omaha Campus School of Pharmacy and Health Professions, Phoenix Campus University Libraries Filter by Department Accounting Accounting and Business Intelligence & Analytics Anesthesiology Anesthesiology (Phoenix) Biology Biomedical Sciences Business Intelligence and Analytics Chemistry and Biochemistry Clinical Research and Public Health Communication Studies Computer Science, Design and Journalism Cultural and Social Studies Dean's Office - Arts & Sciences Economics and Finance Education Emergency Medicine Emergency Medicine (Phoenix) Endodontics English ENT Exercise Science and Pre-Health Professions Family and Community Medicine Family and Community Medicine (Phoenix) Fine & Performing Arts General Dentistry Health Professions History Interdisciplinary Studies Law Marketing and Management Mathematics Med. Microbiology & Immunology Medical Education Medical Education (Phoenix) Medical Humanities Medical Humanities (Phoenix) Medicine Medicine (Phoenix) Modern Languages and Literatures Neurological Surgery Neurological Surgery (Phoenix) Neurology Neurology (Phoenix) Nursing - Bachelors Nursing - Doctorate Nursing - Masters Obstetrics & Gynecology Obstetrics & Gynecology (Phoenix) Occupational Therapy Occupational Therapy (Phoenix) Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Oral Biology Oral Health Promotion Orthopaedic Surgery (Omaha) Orthopaedic Surgery (Phoenix) Paramedicine Pathology Pathology (Phoenix) Pediatric Dentistry Pediatrics Pediatrics (Phoenix) Periodontics Pharmacology and Neuroscience Pharmacy Practice Pharmacy Practice (Phoenix) Pharmacy Sciences Philosophy Physical Therapy Physical Therapy (Phoenix) Physics Political Science and International Relations Prosthodontics Psychiatry Psychiatry (Phoenix) Psychological Science Radiology Radiology (Phoenix) Surgery Surgery (Phoenix) Surgical Services Theology Urology Close Menu All Positions / Faculty Assistant Dean for Evaluation & Analytics -School of Medicine Apply now Description The Assistant Dean for Evaluation & Analytics supports the evaluation and analytic work of School of Medicine initiatives related to program evaluation, accreditation, strategic planning, and quality improvement activities as part of the Office of Accreditation and Quality Improvement. In order to enhance the institutional effectiveness of the School of Medicine in its varied academic missions, the Assistant Dean is responsible for direct supervision for a team responsible for data infrastructure, data visualization, evaluation strategy, and student assessment. The Assistant Dean is expected to contribute to the School’s growing portfolio of education research. The position is a key member of the School of Medicine leadership team. Position Assignment: 1.0 FTE · Overall oversight of all academic data analytics for the School of Medicine · Support and provide oversight for program evaluation of the medical education program to the standards as established by the LCME and physician assistant program to the standards as established by the ARC-PA · Support of the Graduate Medical Education Offices data analytics · School of Medicine program evaluation for university accreditation · Collaboration with relevant university officials on university-scope data analytics initiatives · Oversight of the development and implementation of student assessment for the medical education program · Participation and leadership in faculty and learner pedagogical scholarship and research · Participation and guidance for the Evaluation Committee (a subcommittee of the medical education program Education Program Committee) · Supervision of staff in the Office of Accreditation and Quality Improvement · Serves on University and School of Medicine committees as requested · Coordination of Quality Improvement programming in the Office of Accreditation and Quality Improvement · Development of outcome evaluation for School of Medicine Strategic Plan · Coordination of School of Medicine mistreatment data repository and committee · Leadership in data governance in the School of Medicine and participation in university data governance efforts Qualifications Terminal degree Qualification for faculty appointment at the level of assistant professor or higher Increasing record of experience and responsibility for program evaluation, analytics, and/or assessment in academic medicine Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Five years’ experience in medical school (or equivalent) administrative and leadership positions related to data analytics in the health sciences. Ability to communicate effectively, orally and in writing, excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to work cooperatively with colleagues, leaders and staff at all levels, and the ability to work independently are all desired attributes for this position. Application Instructions Equal Employment Opportunity Statement AAP/EEO Statement Creighton University is committed to providing a safe and non-discriminatory educational and employment environment. The University admits qualified students, hires qualified employees and accepts patients for treatment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, marital status, national origin, age, disability, citizenship, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, or other status protected by law. Its education and employment policies, scholarship and loan programs, and other programs and activities, are administered without unlawful discrimination. Department School of Medicine Posted Tue, 10/20/2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying Creighton University uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter Close Sidebar ID Internal Resources Directory Office 365 BlueLine NEST Libraries Bookstore myCreighton Online Ministries Site Index Get In Touch Contact Creighton Jobs Maps & Directions Media Inquiries Locations Omaha, NE Phoenix, AZ 2500 California Plaza Omaha, NE 68178 402.280.2700 Image Translate © Creighton University\t2026 Legal / Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Statement Web Accessibility Statement LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube © Creighton University\t2026 LinkedIn Facebook Instagram Youtube"
